{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover/lean4/pulls/15531","id":4769387972,"node_id":"PR_kwDOB7kabM8AAAABHEcVxA","html_url":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/15531","diff_url":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/15531.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/15531.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover/lean4/issues/15531","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover/lean4/pulls/15531/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover/lean4/pulls/15531/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover/lean4/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover/lean4/issues/15531/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover/lean4/statuses/5b76244dd0a3a58c5090de56edfc48c182808420","number":15531,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"perf: share the mapping when an `.olean` is loaded again in one process","user":{"login":"casavaca","id":96765450,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcSGCg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96765450?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/casavaca","html_url":"https://github.com/casavaca","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casavaca/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casavaca/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casavaca/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casavaca/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casavaca/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casavaca/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casavaca/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casavaca/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casavaca/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR makes a repeated load of an `.olean` within one process reuse the existing mapping instead of copying the file to the heap and relocating all its pointers. This happens on every repeated import, e.g. in the REPL and in Lake when lakefiles have different imports.\n\nCloses #3826\n\nWhile a mapping of a file is alive, mapping it again at its fixed `base_addr` fails, so the reader falls back to `malloc` + `read` + a fixup walk. This PR records mappings that landed at their `base_addr`, and a later load of the same file gets a new `CompactedRegion` for that mapping; `lean_compacted_region_free` unmaps it when the last user is freed.\n\nWhy this is sound: a shared mapping must hold exactly the bytes of its file for as long as it is shared, so nothing may write to it.\n- The file is the same one: it is identified by `st_dev`/`st_ino` (plus size and mtime), the live mapping keeps the inode alive, and `lean_compacted_region_save` replaces files by renaming.\n- Loading writes nothing: pointer fixups only happen when the file or one of its dep regions did not land at its `base_addr`, and closure relocation only in `v3` files, so only `v2` files loaded with all dep regions in place are shared. Their dep regions stay in place while they are shared, since dep regions are loaded and freed together with their dependents.\n- Using the data writes nothing: compacted objects are persistent, so reference counting skips them, and thunks and tasks are stored with their values.\n- That leaves `IO.Ref`s (even reading one exchanges its value) and `IO.Promise`s, and these have never been used in `v2` files. The compactor supports them for completeness (`IO.Ref` since it was added in 2019, `IO.Promise` since #6958 gave it its own object kind); the only files that contain them are `--incr-load` snapshots (#13965, #14106), which are `v3`; and none of the 28,750 region loads of `import Lean Lake` that went through the fixup walk contained one. So this PR makes `CompactedRegion.save` reject them unless `allowClosures := true`, as it already does for closures, which turns \"not used\" into \"not possible\".\n\nMeasurements (Linux x86-64, 4656f09f with and without this PR):\n- `importModules #[`Lean]` repeated in one process: 2.0–2.9 s and +1.5–2.1 GB RSS per repeated import → 0.38–0.42 s and +50–65 MB.\n- `lake env true` with two lakefiles importing `Lake` and `Lake` + `Lean.Server.References` (the case in the issue): 1.30 s / 1.78 GB → 0.61 s / 0.92 GB.\n- A single `import Lean`: unchanged (0.76–0.80 s).\n- REPL built against 606c89b9, four commands starting with `import Lean`: commands 2–4 took 2.3–3.6 s each, RSS up to 7.1 GB → 0.6 s each, 1.84 GB.\n\nWindows keeps the current behavior, since `fstat` has no inode number there.\n\nTest: `tests/compile/shared_mapping.lean` (fails without the change). The full test suite passes locally.\n\nRejecting `IO.Ref`s and `IO.Promise`s changes what can be stored in an `.olean`. Is that acceptable, or would you rather keep `v2` as is and have only the module-data readers opt into sharing?\n\n---\nDrafted with Claude Opus 5.5\n","labels":[{"id":5906657964,"node_id":"LA_kwDOB7kabM8AAAABYBByrA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover/lean4/labels/toolchain-available","name":"toolchain-available","description":"A toolchain is available for this PR, at leanprover/lean4-pr-releases:pr-release-NNNN","color":"366329","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-07T07:26:38Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T03:43:38Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"982132234164bc2ed53854c4502dce000c6fefc5","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"casavaca:share-olean-mappings","ref":"share-olean-mappings","repo":{"id":1383698040,"node_id":"R_kgDOUnmOeA","name":"lean4","full_name":"casavaca/lean4","owner":{"login":"casavaca","id":96765450,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcSGCg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96765450?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.g